        "original_id": "ee84b9d2-259b-59dd-b2f7-9f33076d9f4d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: 1930 Ashes series\n- People: Bill Woodfull, Percy Chapman, Bob Wyatt\n- Roles: Australia captain, England captain\n- Topics: Australian cricket team in England in 1930, Bill Woodfull\n\nFacts:\n- William Maldon \"Bill\" Woodfull was an Australian cricketer who lived from 22 August 1897 to 11 August 1965 and played in the 1920s and 1930s.\n- Bill Woodfull captained the Australian tourists in England in 1930.\n- Percy Chapman captained England in the 1930 Ashes series before being dropped in favour of Bob Wyatt for the final Test.\n- Australia won the 1930 Ashes series against England by winning two Tests, losing one, and drawing two.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
